WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.540
At 75 beats a minute, one full
heartbeat lasts just 0.8 seconds.

2
00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:10.800
In that time, every valve in
your heart opens and shuts once,

3
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.490
in strict order.

4
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.890
Get the timing wrong, and
blood would flow backwards.

5
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.240
Yet your heart has no switches.

6
00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:22.900
So how does each valve open and
close at exactly the right moment?

7
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.890
In this mission, you'll trace blood
through the heart's four chambers and two

8
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:30.030
pumps, from the veins to the arteries.

9
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.720
Then you'll follow one
complete beat, stage by stage,

10
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:35.780
and watch every valve.

11
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:40.820
Your mission: explain how your heart's
valves open and close at exactly the right

12
00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:41.560
moments.
